# === dsh-deepartments patch: dsh-app-boot watchUserPatchLayers (R3) ===
#
# WHAT THIS FIXES
#   Only the profile's own cordis.patch.yml and the home-level file were
#   watched live; a bundle-layer knob (e.g. a dshd-core row in a bundle's
#   cordis.patch.yml) silently stayed inactive until a daemon restart. This
#   patch adds watchUserPatchLayers (watch EVERY patch-layer file: bundle
#   layers required=true, then profile, then home; dedupe by resolved path;
#   one transactional refresh; disposer drains on failure) and refactors
#   watchUserPatches as a single-file wrapper. ADAPTATIONS to rc.2 (skew):
#   the runtime export list lacks DEFAULT_PROFILE_PATCH_RELOAD (upstream drift)
#   — only watchUserPatchLayers was added to it; the d.ts keeps the runtime's
#   10 drift lines (header, export list, 2 doc lines).
